--TEST--
`+` and `+=` with an array operand do not compile, and the diagnostic names the member that replaced them — `rule:types/array-combination`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// PHP's array union operator is removed rather than migrated, so there is no
// silent behaviour change to fall into: the operator stops compiling, and
// both spellings are reported from the same run.
array<int> $a = [1, 2];
array<int> $b = [3, 4];
echo Core\Arr::count($a + $b), "\n";
$a += $b;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0467]: `+` is not defined with an array operand
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
